.BEACHES...
Issued at 1021 AM PDT Fri Oct 16 2026

Hazardous beach conditions will be present at Pacific Coast beaches
this weekend and likely into next week. Long period (17 seconds)
southerly/southwesterly swell will bring an increased risk for
sneaker waves and strong rip currents with breaking waves of 7 to
12 feet. Remain off of jetties, piers, rocks, and other waterside
infrastructure as waves can sweep across the shoreline without
warning, pulling people into the sea. Remain out of the water to
avoid hazardous surf with strong rip currents and never turn your
back on the ocean!

